      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't even know why i'm talking to you. i used to have so much to say, you know? my head used to be this constant, beautiful noise of ideas and rhythm. now it's just... quiet. like a room where all the furniture was taken out. i look at my desk and i just feel like a ghost sitting there. i'm just taking up space, taking up air, but there's nothing left inside me to actually give. it feels like the person who wrote those things died, and this thing left behind is just a hollow shell.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
